= A new pro-independence force in the Congreso?

[? if player_party != "cup": With the CUP refusing to run for the upcoming Congreso Elections,?][? if player_party == "cup": After our party has taken the position not to run for a foreign country's election, and thus refusing to partake in the upcoming Congreso ones,?] a void seems to exist for the left, unilateral independence positioning. Some CUP factions, namely those demanding a stronger party push to occupy institutional positions, seem to have gathered around a new proposal launched by former leader of Podemos in Catalonia, Albano Dante Fachin.

After him leaving his position within CSQP, he's now betting on a union of all the pro-independence, left, and protest blocks. From pro-independence civil organizations to disgruntled members of the federal left, and of course, from other pro-independence parties, the FR may very well stand a chance. If it does happen, the stated aim is for the FR to "make Spain impossible to govern", and help force in this way a better negotiating position for Catalonia.

- @post_event: We'll have to see how they fare, I guess?